    "node_002": {
      "text": "There is a dog who watches from the porch. Not guarding, not waiting , just knowing. Duke has seen the man pass through the yard again, feet bare against the cooling earth. Tyler. The name settles in his broad skull like a stone in still water. He does not rise. He does not follow. He breathes slow and even, eyes half lidded against the fading light, holding the world exactly as it is. Some things do not need chasing. Some things only need witnessing.",
